# The engine's portable modules: everything on the host side of src/plat.h.
#
# Read by two things that must not disagree about it -- tools/harness/run.sh,
# which links it into every harness that needs the whole engine, and
# probe/Makefile, which links it into the probes that load a real script.
# It used to be spelled out in run.sh alone; probe/sccheck.c and
# probe/stmtdump.c said "<parse chain>" in their build instructions and left
# the reader to reconstruct it.
#
# A list like this going one entry short is not a loud failure. The harness
# README records that it happened: the suite came back with "failures" that
# were only a missing source, and a missing engine module presents as a link
# error at best and as a stub being linked instead of the real thing at
# worst (see vbedos.c, which compiles to three do-nothing functions off the
# DOS target). One copy, therefore.
#
# Not here, and deliberately:
#   main.c       linked by no harness and no probe; it is the frame loop
#   platw32.c    the Win32 side of the seam; the host uses
#                tools/hostshim/plathost.c
#   present.c    likewise, with tools/hostshim for what a harness needs
#                -- and for video that is tools/hostshim/presenthost.c, which
#                run.sh links alongside movie.c the way it links wavehost.c
#                alongside audio.c
#   wavedos.c    compiles to a sink off the DOS target; harnesses drive
#   vbedos.c     tools/hostshim/wavehost.c instead
#
# input.c and scale.c *are* here. They look like platform code and are not:
# what a key or a click means is portable, and scale.c comes along for
# mr_fit_map_point.
#
# One module per line. Blank lines and # comments are ignored; the readers
# prepend src/ and append .c.

save
history
serial
stmtid
expr
interp
scene
vfs
lex
parse
style
slang
slparse
image
png
# CPUID, which gates both MMX kernels. Here, and *not* beside yuvmmx.c and
# blendmmx.c in the "cannot be built on the host" list, because it genuinely
# can be: it has a gcc path over <cpuid.h>. That matters -- the module now
# standing between the engine and its two fast paths should not also be the
# one nothing can link. gfx.c and yuv.c both call into it from have_simd().
cpu
gfx
audio
font
ui
# The composited dialogue strip, kept between typing frames. Here rather than
# inside ui.c because the policy that decides when a strip is still good lives
# in the frame loop, and bandtest drives both halves.
bandcache
slrender
mp3impl
# Video. plmimpl.c instantiates pl_mpeg and is C99 -- the makefiles give it
# -za99, as they do mp3impl.c -- so it is a translation unit of its own.
# yuv.c is the conversion and is pure; movie.c is the player and calls
# mr_present_video, which is why presenthost.c exists.
#
# Two codecs, picked from the file's own bytes. viddec.c is the dispatch and
# is the only thing movie.c includes; plmimpl.c is MPEG-1 in a program
# stream, and avi.c plus xviddec.c are MPEG-4 in an AVI. See viddec.h for why
# both are kept.
#
# **xviddec.c drags in xvidcore**, which no other harness needed and which is
# not an engine source: run.sh builds it as a cached host library when it
# sees this file in the list (mkxvidhost.sh), and the Makefile links the
# Watcom one. That is the only entry here with a dependency outside src/.
plmimpl
avi
xviddec
viddec
yuv
movie
# pack.c turns a 32bpp surface into the display's pixel format. It is here
# because yuv.c calls mr_pack_is_bgra32: mr_yuv_rows_fused writes display
# pixels straight into the framebuffer and has to ask whether that is sound
# for the current format. Until then nothing portable needed it and only
# packtest and the two presenters linked it -- the engine list going one
# entry short is exactly the failure this file's header warns about, and it
# presented as 53 harnesses failing to link at once.
pack
tl
datefmt
input
scale
md5
persist
musicroom
pyfn
rhythm
list
config
ansi
